Appendix G. Falsification Thresholds and Pre-Registration

The thesis pre-registers the following decision thresholds.

Condition 1 (definition). If the DVA decomposition shows that the domestic lifecycle service annuity in the stadium vertical-mobility package is already held by Moroccan firms at a level above the pilot threshold, the premise of foreign-specialist capture is false. The pilot threshold is stated as a numeric share in the measurement manual before data collection; it is not adjusted after the fact.

Condition 2 (cost gap). If the landed-cost gap between a Moroccan maintenance entrant and the OEM exceeds 15% across two consecutive procurement cycles, the preference instrument is insufficient, and the thesis must recommend a different entry segment or a different instrument.

Condition 3 (audit). If the inspection-game condition pF > g cannot be satisfied because audit capacity is unavailable or penalties are not enforceable, the pilot is not feasible, and the thesis must report the infeasibility as a finding.

These thresholds are fixed in advance. Any post-hoc adjustment is reported as a deviation from the pre-registration.

