Appendix I. Case Selection Justification

The Grand Stade Hassan II is selected as the primary forensic case because the vertical-mobility award is recent, attributable, and structurally comparable to a repeatable pipeline. The Mohammed VI Tower is used only as a budget-drift case because no public contract-level account separates its component costs, and its headline figures are corrupted in secondary circulation. The stadium’s domestic-major civil packages and foreign-specialist vertical-mobility package provide the identification contrast. The repeatable housing or public-building pipeline is selected because volume, not height, tests whether maintenance capability scales. The housing-aid segment of MAD 300,000–700,000 is the test of industrial rather than prestige capability.

