Appendix J. Pilot Rule Operational Manual

J.1 Unbundling

Flagship vertical-mobility contracts are separated into lots for new equipment, installation, maintenance, and modernisation. The service lot is sized so that domestic maintenance firms can bid credibly. Unbundling operates on competition structure, not origin, and is therefore less exposed to legal challenge than an expanded price preference.

J.2 Audited DVA Statement

Every bid above a threshold includes a DVA statement distinguishing DVA-GDP from DVA-GNI. The contracting authority audits a random sample with probability p, and the penalty F includes exclusion under Article 152. The pilot proceeds only if the design satisfies pF > g at the estimated values.

J.3 Open-Diagnostics and Spare-Parts Access

Original equipment contracts include a condition requiring disclosure of diagnostic protocols and non-discriminatory spare-parts pricing to accredited independent service providers. The clause is a condition of the DVA preference. If accepted and enforced, the domestic maintenance market can scale beyond OEM-dependent technicians; if rejected or circumvented, the structural foreclosure persists.

J.4 Payment Discipline

The pilot includes enforceable payment timelines and penalties on the contracting authority, not merely on the contractor. The legal default under Law 69-21 is 60 days from invoice, with late-payment interest at the central-bank rate plus 0.85% per month. Reported averages are lower in ministerial departments (approximately 23 days) and public establishments (under 38 days), but these averages conceal persistent outliers and do not capture small contractors on local-authority projects. In the second quarter of 2026, 28% of construction-sector managers reported difficult cash positions. Without payment discipline, the DVA preference is a nudge on a market that is already discounting the state’s credibility.

J.5 Legal Screening Before Finalisation

The pilot rule is screened against the procurement chapters of Morocco’s free-trade agreements, including the United States–Morocco Free Trade Agreement thresholds, before it is finalised. The amending decree to Decree No. 2-22-431 is the legislative window; the gaps on national preference are the opening for the DVA pilot rule.

